  "conclusion": {
    "claimed_state": "COMPLETE_VERIFIED",
    "summary": "Byte 8 is not the speed. It is a checksum (sum of bytes 9..27 mod 256) that changes whenever the speed byte (10) changes. Changing byte 8 alone makes the engine reject the save; a codec that recomputes it produces edits the engine loads. Bytes 5 and 9 remain unknown and are preserved verbatim."
